## The one carrier of luce-std 0.3 that the compiler's own source uses: a value together with
## the obligation to release it. The seed's programs run once and exit, so what they are
## handed is kept until then; `release` is the call luce-std's callers make, with nothing to
## give back here.

## A value its receiver releases when done with it.
pub struct Owned[T]:
    ## The value.
    pub let value: T

    ## End the receiver's obligation.
    pub func release():
        _ = self
